- skills/replicate/SKILL.md, reproduce
- skills/replicate/references/assessment.md and rules.md for unchanged contracts
- Parent1572 receiving Imagine and replicator df890ef frozen evidence

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Reproduce guidance audits each relevant join using the authors' actual
  keys on inputs at the authors' join stage before checker normalization or
  correction (preserving authors' preceding transformations), recording stage,
  keys, cardinality/duplication, match/unmatched diagnostics and denominators;
  preserve the original result and any separately labelled corrected run.
- [ ] Compare constructed variable definitions and sample rules in text,
  notes/appendices, and code; trace constructed missingness through operations
  and downstream samples. Unknown or conflicting evidence is recorded with
  source anchors as an anomaly, not an automatically established coding error.
- [ ] Evidence and unresolved audit coverage stay visible; author package
  files stay read-only. Findings/candidate corrections reuse existing signed
  probe and author-ruling rules rather than authorizing changed specifications.
- [ ] Person-written signatures, frozen comparison tolerance, existing
  selected-target/whole-paper/ACRe meanings, and report contracts stay unchanged.
  No new scientific run, score exception, default main-result rule, footnote
  scope ruling, or signing mode is introduced.

## Plan and validation

Add bounded generic reproduce guidance and reuse the anomaly/probe contracts;
no new verb, schema, dependency, or paper-specific audit implementation.
Source-read validation checks instructions against the frozen Atanasov
join/construction evidence; do not rerun the numerical case or modify
replicator. Semantic diff and preservation checks fit documentation; do not
add wording tests. Run lint/fast, distinct semantic adherence, gaze, then gate.
Receiving Imagine/Blind-Spot inherited from1572; original-key and contradiction
bounds are load-bearing.

## Author-specified placement (2026-11-27)

Use two binding lines in SKILL.md reproduce, one per audit, linked to a
reference (assessment.md or new data-audit.md). Put join checklist details
there: actual keys, stage-specific match rates/denominators, unmatched-key
sample, encoding/quotes/whitespace/case, many-to-many, duplicate keys, and
missingness in constructed variables. Give a text-versus-code table format.
Keep paper cases outside the harness. The proposed score gate for unaudited
joins is NOT adopted; report audit coverage separately without changing Fully
or other canonical meanings.
